"""Seed species data for Petey Plant.

Starter records covering all 12 archetype rigs and the main families.
No dataset or model weights are downloaded; this file is hand-curated
structured data. The name '10k' refers to the intended scale of a
future ingest (see ingest_json_dump); the full 10,000-record ingest
is NOT shipped, and no outward copy may claim 10k coverage. merged composition (scope-3 verified merge): 76 starter records, of
which 31 carry source-verified qualitative data (18 merged into
existing records + 13 newly added records); numeric care parameters
remain approximate model parameters (see below).
Botanical-engine merge: 79 records after attaching 7 engine nodes and
adding 3 engine records (Thai Constellation cultivar, Goeppertia makoyana,
Phalaenopsis aphrodite); engine numbers are model parameters, never
verified facts (see the merge block below the SPECIES list).

HONESTY — NUMERIC CARE PARAMETERS ARE APPROXIMATE GAME-MODEL
PARAMETERS, NOT MEASURED SPECIES VALUES: crop_coeff_k, moisture %,
VPD kPa, lux, and most soil pH ranges are calibrated to qualitative
care categories (bright indirect / moist / dry) for the game model.
They are NOT published per-species measurements. The only sourced
exceptions noted in this file are Monstera pH 5.5-7.0 and Dionaea
acidic peat ~4.5-5.5 (its pH range is 4.0-5.5 here, i.e. acidic peat).
Qualitative verified guidance lives in the verified_* fields on
records merged from verified_species.json and must be preferred over
the numeric approximations for user-facing care advice.

The common_pathogens field is retained under its historic name
because code reads it (rag_engine.care_chunk), but it actually lists
"common pests & diseases (unverified per species)": its values mix
pests (spider mites, mealybugs, scale insects, aphids, cochineal)
with diseases (root rot, powdery mildew, bacterial spots), and the
per-species entries are unverified. Do not present them as sourced
facts.

FAMILY_TO_ARCHETYPE maps a family to its most typical archetype rig.
Every one of the 12 archetype ids appears as a value in that mapping.
"""
